1
00:00:00,093 --> 00:00:01,308
You're drifting off to sleep.

2
00:00:01,667 --> 00:00:02,280
Eyes heavy.

3
00:00:02,662 --> 00:00:02,962
And then...

4
00:00:02,951 --> 00:00:03,461
you fall.

5
00:00:03,965 --> 00:00:05,342
Your whole body jerks awake.

6
00:00:05,735 --> 00:00:06,337
Heart pounding.

7
00:00:06,841 --> 00:00:08,114
Up to seventy percent of people

8
00:00:08,126 --> 00:00:08,728
get this.

9
00:00:09,225 --> 00:00:10,278
Most people think it's just a

10
00:00:10,278 --> 00:00:10,973
weird dream.

11
00:00:11,501 --> 00:00:13,086
The truth is way stranger.

12
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:14,569
For a split second,

13
00:00:14,962 --> 00:00:16,235
your brain thinks you're falling.

14
00:00:16,641 --> 00:00:17,115
For real.

15
00:00:17,625 --> 00:00:18,493
As you drift off,

16
00:00:18,725 --> 00:00:19,743
your muscles go limp.

17
00:00:20,171 --> 00:00:20,530
Fast.

18
00:00:21,064 --> 00:00:22,557
But your brainstem is still on

19
00:00:22,557 --> 00:00:22,893
guard.

20
00:00:23,275 --> 00:00:24,675
It reads that sudden drop as

21
00:00:24,687 --> 00:00:25,127
a fall.

22
00:00:25,645 --> 00:00:27,520
So it fires an emergency signal

23
00:00:27,716 --> 00:00:29,221
to every muscle at once.

24
00:00:29,733 --> 00:00:31,411
One theory goes back millions of

25
00:00:31,422 --> 00:00:31,955
years.

26
00:00:32,314 --> 00:00:34,235
Our ancestors slept in trees.

27
00:00:34,757 --> 00:00:35,798
One slip meant death.

28
00:00:36,192 --> 00:00:37,673
The ones whose brains jerked them

29
00:00:37,673 --> 00:00:38,067
awake...

30
00:00:38,298 --> 00:00:38,854
survived.

31
00:00:39,384 --> 00:00:40,287
That's why it hits harder when

32
00:00:40,287 --> 00:00:41,016
you're stressed,

33
00:00:41,398 --> 00:00:42,498
wired on caffeine,

34
00:00:42,741 --> 00:00:43,424
or exhausted.

35
00:00:43,952 --> 00:00:44,670
But for some people,

36
00:00:44,681 --> 00:00:45,330
it's not a jolt.

37
00:00:45,688 --> 00:00:46,394
It's a gunshot.

38
00:00:46,776 --> 00:00:47,691
Inside their head.

39
00:00:48,197 --> 00:00:48,683
It's real.

40
00:00:49,053 --> 00:00:49,736
It's harmless.

41
00:00:50,106 --> 00:00:51,484
And nobody fully knows why.

42
00:00:51,997 --> 00:00:53,374
I'll decode that one in part

43
00:00:53,386 --> 00:00:53,721
two.

44
00:00:54,092 --> 00:00:54,879
One body glitch,

45
00:00:55,064 --> 00:00:55,619
every day.

46
00:00:56,071 --> 00:00:56,453
Follow,

47
00:00:56,661 --> 00:00:57,448
so you don't miss it.
